Z||000003||1FieroGTRacingInc||03-31-2000||05:21 PM||||HHHMMmmmm...  Nobody has even a clue of what the problem is or what I can do? 1FGTRInc.||||reg||1
Z||000004||AL||03-31-2000||08:56 PM||||ok this is what you do, pull the thermistat out, bend it enough so it fits in your housing, next put it in a pan with water and boil it, check if it opens and closes,on mine i bent it but i also made sure it wasn't interfering with the open and closing mechanism of the thermistat.||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||03-31-2000||09:33 PM||||looking at the spare 4 cyl neck I have, Only 2 things can cause this. I beleive the V6 uses the same stats.<P>1. the thermostat is out of spec and not seating into the lower neck area properly.<P>2. the lower neck area is damaged or rusted keepint the stat from seating.||||reg||1
Z||000006||1FieroGTRacingInc||03-31-2000||11:59 PM||||Thank you Both...  I will check that 1st thing in morning....         1FGTRInc.||||reg||1
Z||000007||WKDFIRO||04-01-2000||05:19 AM||||With the gasket being new sometimes you have to push a little more to seat the o-ring. It may feel like its seated but push a little more and it should pop into place. ||||reg||1
