Z||000009||Bruce||04-01-2000||04:05 PM||||Rodney,<BR>The Stant 180 degree thermostat is listed as part #13818 at Wrenchhead; it's different when you refer to it with reference to your lower temp. fan swith. I think you have it as 18313. Just a typo, because I want to buy the fan switch.<BR>Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000010||theogre||04-01-2000||04:34 PM||||On those thermostat O rings. coat them very lightly with vaseline. that should help. A little dielectric compound will also work. Just a film of a coating is all you want.<P>rock them a bit as you seat them helps too.||||reg||1
Z||000011||1FieroGTRacingInc||04-01-2000||11:14 PM||||Thank's theorge...  Should I have to bend the top of the thermo. itself to9 get the top cap on??     <BR>                        1FGTRInc.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Patrick||04-01-2000||11:38 PM||||<BR>If you've got to bend the top of the thermostat down for the cap to go on, then you haven't pushed the thermostat down far enough. It sort of snaps into place. Mine was very difficult to get down far enough also. I held a small piece of wood over the top of mine and tapped it gently into place with a hammer.||||reg||1
